  "results": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "mmwr_nwss_coe#4",
      "doc_id": "mmwr_nwss_coe",
      "heading": "MMWR: NWSS Centers of Excellence during the 2022\u201323 respiratory season > Altmetric:",
      "text": "Wastewater surveillance (WWS), the systematic detection of infectious agents in wastewater, provided a valuable tool for monitoring SARS-CoV-2 circulation during the COVID-19 pandemic; surveillance has expanded from 20 to 53 jurisdictions across the United States, with increasing capacity to test for more respiratory pathogens (*1*,*2*). This report highlights the use of wastewater data by the four National Wastewater Surveillance System\u2019s (NWSS) Centers of Excellence (California; Colorado; Houston, Texas; and Wisconsin) to guide public health action during the 2022\u201323 respiratory disease season. This activity was reviewed by CDC, deemed not research, and was conducted consistent with applicable federal law and CDC policy.\\*"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_sources#6",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_sources",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data sources > 3. Wastewater: NWSS",
      "text": "- **Dataset:** CDC Wastewater Viral Activity Level for SARS-CoV-2, Influenza A and RSV.\n- **Publisher:** CDC, National Wastewater Surveillance System (NWSS).\n- **Link:** [atcp-73re](https://data.cdc.gov/Public-Health-Surveillance/CDC-Wastewater-Viral-Activity-Level-for-SARS-CoV-2/atcp-73re)\n- **Releases used:** <!-- auto:releases_nwss -->11<!-- /auto:releases_nwss --> dated downloads, the latest dated <!-- auto:newest_nwss -->2026-10-16<!-- /auto:newest_nwss -->.\n- **Fields used:**\n  - Site-level Wastewater Viral Activity Level (WVAL) and its category\n  - The date each site was included in WVAL reporting\n  - The reported data source, used only for a quality flag"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_methods#17",
      "doc_id": "oad_methods",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData methods > 5. Known limitations",
      "text": "5. **Wastewater activity levels are pathogen-specific indices.** Values are not comparable across pathogens; use the category for comparisons.\n6. **Snapshot of source data.** The latest values reflect CDC releases through <!-- auto:latest_releases -->2026-10-16 (NHSN, NWSS) and 2026-10-14 (NSSP)<!-- /auto:latest_releases -->. Later CDC revisions are not included."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "mmwr_nwss_coe#5",
      "doc_id": "mmwr_nwss_coe",
      "heading": "MMWR: NWSS Centers of Excellence during the 2022\u201323 respiratory season > Implementation and Action",
      "text": "Four CDC-funded NWSS Centers of Excellence were established during 2021\u201322. During 2022\u201323, wastewater sampling covered a large proportion of the sites\u2019 populations: 94% (Houston, Texas), 67% (California), 65% (Colorado), and 50% (Wisconsin). Implementation and data usage varied by locality (Box).\n\n**Public Health Actions at the Local Level**\n\n**Colorado.** To help guide local public health action in Colorado, three Denver sewersheds, covering 1.2 million residents, submitted biweekly wastewater samples. Retrospective analyses indicated that WWS detected enterovirus D68 (EV-D68) \u22641 month before syndromic and clinical laboratory signals. This finding led public health officials in Colorado to implement wastewater testing for EV-D68 as part of the enterovirus surveillance model to provide an early warning system for health care surge planning during respiratory virus season."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_dictionary#20",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_dictionary",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data dictionary > 5. Measures",
      "text": "| `feature_name` | Source | Pathogens | Unit | `definition_status` | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `participation_status` | NSSP (derived) | not_applicable | `categorical_coverage_status` | uncertain | HSA rows only. `reduced_participation` if at least one member county had no facility with recent data in CDC's 2026-08-06 facility map. The same value is applied to every week. |\n| `wastewater_activity_level` | NWSS | covid, influenza, rsv | `wval_index_not_cross_pathogen_comparable` | uncertain | CDC's site-level Wastewater Viral Activity Level. **Not comparable across pathogens**, and use caution comparing across sites. |"
    }
  ]
